<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lao Theung</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lao Theung, 'Lao of the mountain slopes', is a broad Lao category for the mainly Mon-Khmer-speaking peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a>, such as the Khmu, who live chiefly on the middle slopes of the uplands. Regarded as the country's oldest inhabitants, they took part in revolts against French rule, notably the rising in the south led by Ong Kommandam that lasted until 1936. Many later supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lao-theung.jpg" alt="Lao Theung" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tango7174 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LuangNamtha_ThatLuangNamtha7_tango7174.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
